sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0243/0244 task, DECISIONS R1-R4 + 5 (shared SSH identity), metrics.exporter_enable decisions, single-swamp-node. docs/cli/node.mdx#orbit-noderoleadd, docs/reference/node-provisioning.md.
  %% Tightened: flow-tighten 2026-11-02, rules 9, 22 (cfgmgmt behaviors named; their checks are the end check, no file read-back).
  %% status: migrated
  %% command: node:role:add
  %% kind: node.role_add
  %% Rule 23: 2026-11-03 required-only main path.
  %% Pinned Debian downloads use the first ArtifactPin candidate: the durable mirror URL, verified at the pin.
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane M icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as Node 12<br/>gets the role
  participant M as Metrics Node<br/>Prometheus
  CLI->>GW: node:role:add 12 app-dev<br/>Node and role
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit node:role:add 12 app-dev`
  %%> - syntax: `<node> <role> [--converge] [--postgres-process=ID] [--clickhouse-process=ID] [--idempotency-key=KEY] [--json]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the Node, by id or exact name, and the role, such as `app-dev`, `app-prod`, `ingress`, `database`, `websocket`, `analytics`, `ci-runner`, `gateway` or `swamp`
  %%> - for `analytics` only: the PostgreSQL and ClickHouse Processes; in a terminal the CLI asks for them
  %%> Optional flags:
  %%> - `--converge` converges a role the Node already has; that is `node.role_converge`, with its own chart
  %%> - `--postgres-process=ID`, `--clickhouse-process=ID`: required for `analytics` only; they feed the role plan and add no steps of their own
  %%> - `--idempotency-key=KEY` reuses a key to retry the start; `--json` gives machine-readable output
  %%> Who can call it:
  %%> - the `orbit` CLI and the MCP tool send the same request
  Note over GW: Validate, claim the role<br/>role: provisioning · task #5170
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - your Node has an access grant to Node 12
  %%> - Node 12 is an active, managed Linux Node
  %%> - the role is not `vpn` or `router`; those are protected from this command
  %%> - Node 12 doesn't have the role yet, and holds no role it conflicts with, such as `app-prod` beside `app-dev`
  %%> - a singleton role, such as `gateway` or `swamp`, has no holder yet; to move one, use `node:role:relocate`
  %%> - one role operation per Node: the Gateway holds a role lock for Node 12 and waits up to 2 minutes for a busy one, then refuses with `node_role.node_busy`
  %%> Builds:
  %%> - the role plan: packages, files, units, Caddy sites, PHP settings, firewall rules and certificate requests
  %%> - for the `metrics` role, the Prometheus and Grafana container specifications and their systemd units
  %%> - the Metrics fleet change, when Node 12 becomes a selected exporter
  %%> Secrets:
  %%> - role credentials go to the Swamp vault as execution copies; the inputs hold only their key names
  %%> Result:
  %%> - the `app-dev` assignment recorded with status provisioning
  %%> - task #5170 recorded with the full intent
  %%> - nothing has happened on the Node yet
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-node-role-add
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209)
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - the role plan with its files and digests
  %%> - the vault key names of the role credentials
  %%> - Node 12's and the Metrics Node's addresses and SSH host keys; the SSH identity comes from the `swamp` role
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5170
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task number, at once
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show`
  SW->>SW: Write the intent<br/>intent file and assets
  opt role credentials are present
    SW->>SW: Write the private input<br/>vault to mode 0600 files
  end
  opt WebSocket credentials
    SW->>SW: Write WebSocket input<br/>vault to private file
  end
  opt Analytics credentials
    SW->>SW: Write Analytics input<br/>vault to private file
  end
  SW->>SW: Write the playbook input<br/>inventory and host keys
  SW->>N: Read the OS release<br/>SSH argv
  SW->>SW: Require supported Ubuntu<br/>native assert
  opt swamp role
    SW->>N: Install Python venv<br/>native bootstrap
  end
  opt swamp role
    SW->>N: Create Ansible venv<br/>native bootstrap
  end
  opt swamp role
    SW->>N: Write Ansible pin<br/>native bootstrap
  end
  opt swamp role
    SW->>N: Write collection pins<br/>native bootstrap
  end
  opt swamp role
    SW->>N: Install Ansible<br/>native bootstrap
  end
  opt swamp role
    SW->>N: Install collections<br/>native bootstrap
  end
  SW->>N: Apply role prerequisites<br/>Ansible phase: prerequisites
  opt role needs Tool Managers
    SW->>N: Set up Tool Managers<br/>native child workflow
  end
  SW->>N: Apply the role on the Node<br/>Ansible phase: node
  opt Analytics uses local storage
    SW->>N: Open Analytics storage<br/>Ansible phase: storage-firewall
  %%> - for local Analytics storage, retire its previous owned port before applying the admitted port
  end
  opt Analytics needs initialization
    SW->>N: Pull the Analytics image<br/>cfgmgmt docker_image
    SW->>N: Create Analytics database<br/>native SSH argv
    SW->>N: Migrate Analytics database<br/>native SSH argv
    SW->>N: Apply Analytics runtime<br/>native child workflow
    SW->>N: Wait for Analytics<br/>Ansible phase: readiness
  end
  opt role plan needs this action
  SW->>N: Install Swamp<br/>cfgmgmt fetch
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - installs the recipe's pinned Swamp release by SHA-256 at `/usr/local/lib/orbit-swamp/<version>/swamp`, a path no process runs from yet
  end
  opt role plan needs this action
  SW->>N: Keep the running Swamp<br/>SSH argv
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - while `/usr/local/bin/swamp` is still a file, renames it into a new directory under `/usr/local/lib/orbit-swamp` and links the path to the release at once; a rename keeps the inode, so a running serve or worker keeps a binary it can start children from
  %%> Why:
  %%> - replacing the file in place left the running workers on a deleted binary, and every 209 dispatch failed until they restarted
  end
  opt role plan needs this action
  SW->>N: Link Swamp<br/>cfgmgmt link
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - points `/usr/local/bin/swamp`, which serve and the workers run, at the pinned release; a running process keeps the file it started from, and the new release takes effect at its next restart
  end
  opt role plan needs this action
  SW->>N: Apply Swamp identity<br/>SSH argv
  end
  opt role plan needs this action
  SW->>N: Apply Swamp serve<br/>cfgmgmt systemd
  end
  opt role plan needs this action
  SW->>N: Apply Swamp worker unit<br/>cfgmgmt systemd
  end
  opt role plan needs this action
  SW->>N: Start ${{ self.worker }}<br/>cfgmgmt systemd
  end
  opt role plan needs this action
  SW->>N: Check Swamp serve<br/>cfgmgmt systemd
  end
  opt role plan needs this action
  SW->>N: Check Swamp worker unit<br/>cfgmgmt systemd
  end
  opt role plan needs this action
  SW->>N: Check ${{ self.worker }}<br/>cfgmgmt systemd
  end
  opt role plan needs this action
  SW->>N: Check Swamp binary<br/>cfgmgmt fetch
  end
  opt role plan needs this action
  SW->>N: Check Swamp link<br/>cfgmgmt link
  end
  opt role plan needs this action
  SW->>N: Check Swamp identity<br/>cfgmgmt file
  end
  opt role plan needs this action
  SW->>SW: Check Swamp runtime<br/>native assert
  end
  opt role needs certificates
    SW->>GW: Sign role certificates<br/>native child workflow
  end
  opt role changes PHP pools
    SW->>N: Publish PHP pools<br/>native delta publication
  end
  SW->>N: Publish role sites<br/>Ansible phase: publication
  SW->>N: Open the firewall<br/>Ansible phase: firewall
  %%> - repair owned rule shapes and keep specific allows before isolation denies and broad peer trust
  opt role changes DNS
    SW->>N: Publish private DNS<br/>native delta publication
  end
  opt role joins Metrics
    SW->>N: Add the exporters<br/>Ansible phase: exporters
    %%> - apply canonical exporter rules and repair owned service isolation shapes and order
    SW->>M: Publish Prometheus<br/>Ansible phase: prometheus
  end
  SW->>N: Check the role<br/>Ansible phase: check
  %%> Role boundary:
  %%> - node:converge owns the Node observer and Orbit CLI
  %%> - each phase is idempotent; a second run reports zero changes
  alt every step passes
    N-->>SW: role services ready
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the check passed for every part of the role
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway for a result
    Note over GW: Record result<br/>role: active · task succeeded
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the `app-dev` role on Node 12 becomes active, with the digest of each applied part
    %%> - Node 12's exporter is recorded as active, when it joined Metrics
    %%> - task #5170 succeeds
  else a step fails
    N--xSW: exit ≠ 0 or no match
    %%> When:
    %%> - a package, file, unit, Caddy validation, certificate, firewall or check step fails
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    %%> The Gateway reads:
    %%> - which step failed and its error code
    Note over GW: Mark the role failed<br/>converge:STEP · rerun --converge
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the role stays recorded, marked failed at `converge:STEP` with the step's own error code
    %%> - task #5170 fails
    %%> On the Node:
    %%> - finished steps stay; there is no rollback
    %%> - that is safe: every step is idempotent and Caddy is never reloaded with a config that fails validation
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - run `orbit node:role:add 12 app-dev --converge` after fixing the cause
  end
  opt run completed or failed
    SW->>SW: Remove the playbook input<br/>private run folder cleanup
    SW->>N: Remove init containers<br/>best-effort cfgmgmt cleanup
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show #5170
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks for the task's status every 2 seconds until it has ended
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
  end
